{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02440",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.5,
      "end_seconds": 2.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.92,
      "end_seconds": 7.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Hi, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 7.72,
      "end_seconds": 11.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.35,
      "end_seconds": 20.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together. Start wherever you like, I'm listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 26.17,
      "end_seconds": 34.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "it's cramping in my calves when I walk, doctor she didn't want to come, but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.43,
      "end_seconds": 39.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.65,
      "end_seconds": 42.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "for about two weeks, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.54,
      "end_seconds": 49.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.4,
      "end_seconds": 57.48,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "It's worse with walking. Moderate, I'd say. It happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.13,
      "end_seconds": 62.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Has there been hair loss on your shins too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.73,
      "end_seconds": 74.89,
      "duration_seconds": 12.16,
      "text": "Yeah, um, that too. I've also had cold feet. Oh, and a slow-healing toe sore. That's been about the same, two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.83,
      "end_seconds": 84.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "Have you had cramping in your calves when you walk before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.47,
      "end_seconds": 95.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "A bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.45,
      "end_seconds": 98.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "What about chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.52,
      "end_seconds": 101.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "No, no chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.9,
      "end_seconds": 106.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Any back pain, fever or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.48,
      "end_seconds": 112.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "I haven't had back pain, fever or pain at rest, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.07,
      "end_seconds": 116.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.62,
      "end_seconds": 119.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.54,
      "end_seconds": 125.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.84,
      "end_seconds": 143.61,
      "duration_seconds": 16.77,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.55,
      "end_seconds": 147.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.18,
      "end_seconds": 150.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "okay, so no allergies at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 152.72,
      "end_seconds": 160.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "Actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to amoxicillin before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.03,
      "end_seconds": 165.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.25,
      "end_seconds": 173.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.89,
      "end_seconds": 182.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "I have diabetes, for about a year. I've got high cholesterol. I've had migraines, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.57,
      "end_seconds": 190.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Right, so high cholesterol and migraines are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.57,
      "end_seconds": 206.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.67,
      "end_seconds": 214.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "I had a mole taken off my arm a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.71,
      "end_seconds": 231.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 232.57,
      "end_seconds": 236.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "She takes sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.0,
      "end_seconds": 241.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 242.21,
      "end_seconds": 243.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Two months now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 246.57,
      "end_seconds": 257.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.94,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature 36.8, BP is 123 over 70, pulse is 70 beats a minute. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.22,
      "end_seconds": 259.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.7,
      "end_seconds": 266.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.64,
      "end_seconds": 281.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.99,
      "end_seconds": 284.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.58,
      "end_seconds": 302.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "The pulses at the left foot are absent and and the foot is cool and shiny."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.58,
      "end_seconds": 319.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "you can relax now. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is peripheral arterial disease. Another possibility is a nerve problem"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.05,
      "end_seconds": 324.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I mean, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.14,
      "end_seconds": 341.65,
      "duration_seconds": 16.51,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with peripheral arterial disease do well once it's treated properly. We should do an ultrasound of the leg arteries for claudication. An ankle-brachial index is what I'd like next, for claudication."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.48,
      "end_seconds": 343.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.83,
      "end_seconds": 360.59,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "I'll start you on clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day, long term that should help with arterial disease one warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse in that case don't wait"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.38,
      "end_seconds": 364.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.22,
      "end_seconds": 372.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Let's plan a check in four weeks. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.25,
      "end_seconds": 377.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.87,
      "end_seconds": 381.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}